    {
     "attrs": [
      {
       "attr": "customData",
       "from": {
        "author": "agent",
        "kind": "entity",
        "role": "node",
        "tooltip": "The settings snapshot is the load-bearing attribute — it is why a rerun can be compared to an original instead of replacing it.\n\n**stale sources** is run-level, which is today's answer, not the wanted one. You want it on the Signal (only the sentiment ones are stale; insider-cluster is perfectly fresh) and it has not been costed. Written down here so the gap is visible rather than remembered."
       },
       "to": {
        "author": "agent",
        "kind": "entity",
        "role": "node",
        "tooltip": "The settings snapshot is why a rerun can be compared to an original instead of replacing it.\n\n**Known over-claim:** after a partial rerun the snapshot describes the whole day when it only describes a quarter of it. That is an accident of how it was built, not a design — see the scoring time now on Signal.\n\n**stale sources** is run-level, which is today's answer and not the wanted one."
       }
      }
     ],
     "id": "pipeline-run",
     "op": "mod"
    },
    {
     "attrs": [
      {
       "attr": "height",
       "from": 80,
       "to": 100
      },
      {
       "attr": "customData",
       "from": {
        "author": "agent",
        "kind": "entity",
        "role": "node",
        "tooltip": "Confidence is gated at 0.70 — below it, the Signal exists internally but reaches nothing a client sees.\n\nSo 'published' is a third state this box does not yet carry."
       },
       "to": {
        "author": "agent",
        "kind": "entity",
        "role": "node",
        "tooltip": "**'scored at' is mine, and it is a direct consequence of the partial-rerun finding.**\n\nA single-pipeline rerun re-scores one pass and leaves the other three alone, so a run's Signals can come from two different moments. In the model as drawn, that situation was *unrepresentable* — which is a decent explanation of how it went unnoticed for so long.\n\nWith a scoring time on the Signal, mixed provenance becomes something the system can state instead of something it merely does."
       }
      }
     ],
